<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Confederation of the Equator</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1824</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Confederation of the Equator was a short-lived republican and separatist revolt in northeastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in 1824, centred on Pernambuco. It arose in opposition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-i-of-brazil">Emperor Pedro I</a>'s centralising constitution. The revolt was suppressed, but it showed the turbulence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>'s founding decade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-equator.jpg" alt="Confederation of the Equator" width="320" height="134" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leandro Martins · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Confederacao_equador_1824_exercito_imperial.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
